# Research participation
Do you want to be involved in the ROBUST research itself? 

## Household surveys
Household surveys of those living near the shared electric mobility hubs in Letterkenny, Galway, Wateford and Dundrum will be undertaken in Summer 2026.  More details comming soon - or just keep an eye out for details in your mailbox. 

## Focus groups and Co-design workshops

The hubs will serve as an incubator, accelerating the uptake of electric mobility options by allowing interacting with future mobility technologies and removing barriers through participatory research. Various stakeholders will be engaged in the process of hub evolution through stakeholder workshops and co-creation workshops. The workshops with various groups of stakeholders will be used for relationships building, knowledge exchange and evaluation of progress and its direction. The co-creation workshops will be organized multiple times during the trial to involve actors in the development of the hubs; where main focus will be placed on frequent hub users to involve them in the recruitment process of trial participants and empower them to become the leaders of bottomup initiatives. The knowledge obtain from multi-actor participation will then be translated into tangible solutions for hub implementation and disseminated in the form of toolkit for policymakers and booklets for communities giving insights into the impact of travel behaviour change.

Sign up for our user newsletter above and stay tuned for further details about forthcoming focus groups and co-design workshops. 

## Toolkit for replicating hubs, and a tooolbox for policymakers: 
The toolkit for replicating hubs will define the criteria for successful implementation of shared-mobility networks and will be a result of multidisciplinary work. The first generation of shared mobility solutions has proven to be attractive to users so far. However, the lack of sufficient expertise, guidelines and tools available for adequate design and standard resulted in cancelled projects, compromised safety and reduced life cycle of vehicles (Frank et al., 2021). 

The toolbox for transport trial appraisal will be developed to allow policymakers to evaluate innovative solutions and benchmark their performance. The toolbox would update the recent appraisal document used by the Department of Transport by incorporating the newest development in the transport field

Practitioners and policymakers can sign up to our research-focussed newsletter for further details and announcements about the toolkit, toolbox and other outputs of the project.

